# Super Mario 3D World: read by launch.sh before the start.
# The game takes Wii Remotes beside the GamePad and Pro Controllers: a real Wii Remote (kernel driver hid-wiimote) is
# read directly and reaches the game as a Wii Remote (held sideways: 2 = jump / confirm, 1 = run, A, B, +, D-pad,
# shake). The game drops all remotes at its title screen, as on the Wii U: the first button press connects the remote
# again, the next one counts. Every other controller stays GamePad / Pro Controller.
export CAFE_WIIMOTE=real
# Fallback when the remote cannot be read directly: a pad held sideways with 2 = A (jump), 1 = Y (run), A = R, B = B.
export WIIU_REMOTE_PAD=quer
# 28 November: guest memory to the GPU as dma-buf (cheaper submissions: frames over 25 ms in 170 s of play 31 -> 11).
export TTT2_GUEST_DMABUF=1
